OL,3,GNEWSAFinal phase of beach protection
OL,4,Awork under way
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe final phase of a major coastal
OL,7,Fprotection project is nearing
OL,8,Fcompletion.
OL,10,FThree three timber groynes west of
OL,11,FBoscombe Pier are being replaced as
OL,12,Fpart of the 10-year Poole Bay Beach
OL,13,FManagement Scheme, which has already
OL,14,Fseen 50 renewed along the seafront.
OL,16,FEach groyne is around 75m (250ft) long,
OL,17,Fwith its foundations extending about
OL,18,Ffive metres (16ft) below the beach.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
